{
  "title": "Capitellum Fractures",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1023/capitellum-fractures",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 18 2023",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Capitellum Fractures are traumatic intra-articular elbow injuries involving the distal humerus at the capitellum.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made using plain radiographs of the elbow.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be nonoperative for nondisplaced fractures but any displacement generally requires anatomic open reduction and internal fixation.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "1% of elbow fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**6% of all distal humerus fractures**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mechanism of injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "typically, low-energy fall on outstretched hand",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "direct, **axial compression with the elbow in a semi-flexed position** creates shear forces",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "radiocapitellar joint is an important static stabilizer of the elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "capitellar fracture can cause **potential block to motion and instability** due to loss of the radiocapitellar articulation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "concomitant injuries to **radial head** and/or **LUCL** can occur up to 60% of the time",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiocapitellar articulation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "essential to longitudinal and valgus stability of the elbow",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "can also lead to coronal plane instability with capitellar excision if medial structures are not intact",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "integral relationship with the posterolateral ligamentous complex of the elbow (i.e. LUCL)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Classification",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "**Bryan and Morrey Classification (with McKee modification)**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type I",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Large osseous piece of the capitellum involved",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Can involve trochlea",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/hahn%20steinthal%203.jpg",
                          "caption": "This is a lateral elbow radiograph showing a capitellar fracture."
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/hahn%20steinthal%201a.jpg",
                          "caption": "Biplanar radiographs of a Hahn-Steinthal capitellar fracture."
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/hahn%20steinthal%201b.jpg",
                          "caption": "Radiographs of a Hahn-Steinthal injury after fixation."
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type II",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Kocher-Lorenz fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Shear fracture of articular cartilage",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Articular cartilage separation with very little subchondral bone attached",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/kocher%20lorenz.jpg",
                          "caption": "Lateral radiograph, elbow, showing a capitellar fracture."
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type III",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Broberg-Morrey fracture",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Severely comminuted",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Multifragmentary",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/type%20iii.jpg",
                          "caption": "This is an example of a type III capitellum fracture."
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Type IV",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "McKee modification",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Coronal shear fracture that includes the capitellum and trochlea",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/capitellum%20lateral%20type%20iv%20example.jpg",
                          "caption": "Lateral radiograph, elbow"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**fall on outstretched arm** (typically fall from standing)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "typically, elbow is in semi-flexed elbow position",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "elbow pain, deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "swelling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "wrist pain may also occur",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection and palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ecchymosis, swelling",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "diffuse tenderness",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "range of motion & instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may have **mechanical block to flexion/extension and/or rotation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "neurovascular exam",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral of the elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "best demonstrated on **lateral radiograph**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/lateral_elbow_xray.jpg",
                          "caption": "lateral radiograph"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "**\"double arc\" sign created from subchondral bone of capitellum and lateral part of trochlea**",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "5",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "delineates fracture anatomy and classification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/hahn%20steinthal%202.jpg",
                  "caption": "Series of images showing a Hahn-Steinthal capitellar fracture."
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "posterior splint immobilization for < 3 weeks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**nondisplaced Type I** fractures (<2 mm displacement)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**nondisplaced Type II** fractures (<2 mm displacement)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open reduction and internal fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**displaced Type I fractures** (>2 mm displacement)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**Type IV fractures**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**ORIF with lateral column approach**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "indications",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "isolated capitellar fractures",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "type IV fractures that can have trochlear involvement",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**ORIF with posterior approach with or without olecranon osteotomy**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "indications",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "capitellar fractures with associated fractures/injuries to distal humuers/olecranon and/or medial side of the elbow",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "arthroscopic-assisted ORIF",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**isolated type I fractures with good bone stock**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "fragment excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "displaced Type II fractures (>2 mm displacement)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "displaced Type III fractures (>2 mm displacement)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "total elbow arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "unreconstructable capitellar fractures in **elderly patients with associated medial column instability**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**ORIF with lateral column approach**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**lateral approach recommended for isolated Type I and Type IV fx**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**supine positioning**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**lateral skin incision centered over the lateral epicondyle** extending to 2cm distal to the radial head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/approaches.jpg",
                      "caption": "approaches"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**headless screw fixation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "minifragment screw using posterior to anterior fixation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "counter sink screw using anterior to posterior fixation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/hahn%20steinthal%202.jpg",
                          "caption": "Series of images showing a Hahn-Steinthal capitellar fracture."
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "mini-fragment or capitellar plates can be used to capture fractures with proximal extension",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/ap_capitellar_plate.jpg",
                      "caption": "capitellar fracture"
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/lateral_capitellar_plate.jpg",
                      "caption": "lateral capitellar plate"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**avoid disruption of the blood supply** that comes from the posterolateral aspect of the elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**do not destabilize LUCL**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**ORIF with posterior approach with or without olecranon osteotomy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indicated when **more extensive articular work** is needed",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/ct_scan_elbow.jpg",
                      "caption": "ct scan elbow"
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/ct_scan_elbow_postop.jpg",
                      "caption": "postop with olecranon osteotomy"
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/ct_scan_elbow_postop2.jpg",
                      "caption": "ct scan elbow"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can also be used when **concomitant medial sided injuries and/or distal humeral fractures** require more fixation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**lateral decubitus positioning**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "long-posterior based incision along the elbow",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**radial and ulnar based flaps** allow access to both medial and lateral sides of elbow",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fracture-pattern specific",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "independent headless compression/cannulated screws for capitellar component",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "supplemental fixation for concomitant pathology",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "parallel or orthoogonal distal humerus plates",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "radial head arthroplasty/ORIF",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "LUCL/UCL repair via bone tunnels or suture anchors",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Arthroscopic-assisted ORIF**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "definitive indications not fully known",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "experienced arthroscopists, **indicated for isolated capitellar fractures**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "supine or lateral positioning (dependent on desire for anterior or posterior access)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/scope_position_1.jpg",
                      "caption": "positioning for scope"
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/scope_position_2.jpg",
                      "caption": "positioning for scope"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**70 degree scope** can be helpful in gaining access",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "can be combined with limited open technique for fracture manipulation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "standard portals (anteromedial, anterolateral, posterolateral)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "proximal anterolateral portal established under fluoroscopic guidance to place trocar to allow for reduction of fracture fragment",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/trochar_move.jpg",
                      "caption": "intraoperative image"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "extend elbow and push fragment with trocar for reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "flex radial head past 90 to lock reduction",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "anteromedial and posterolateral portals allow for fracture debridement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "freer elevator can help maintain reduction while cannulated/headless compression screws are placed under fluoroscopic guidance (typically posterior to anterior in direction)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/1023/images/cannulated_screws_scope.jpg",
                      "caption": "scope assisted screws"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Elbow contracture/stiffness (most common)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Nonunion (1-11% with ORIF)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Ulnar nerve injury**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Heterotopic ossification (4% with ORIF)**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**AVN of capitellum**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Nonunion of olecranon osteotomy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Instability**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Post-traumatic arthritis**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Cubital valgus**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Tardy ulnar nerve palsy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Infection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Most patients will gain functional range of motion but have **residual stiffness**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Surgical treatment results are generally favorable",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "reoperation rates as high as 48% (mostly due to stiffness)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Posterior comminution has been associated with significantly worse functional outcomes and higher complication rates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
